TO : USG, ASG, WSG, NSG
CC : CEC, SSC, CDA, CCA, CCE, CCM, CTY, CTS, TMO
FM : CCB

[WK46 Back-Haul Performance Summary]

[cid:362B.gif@12345678.87654321]


● TPS :

1. TTL L/F: 54%
- PSX USSEA add call/ AWS and AWY lane merging/ seasonal cargo volume increase have effected showing high L/F

2. By lane

1) PS: L/F: 47%
- PSX lane: L/F 52%
- PSX lane volume has increased around 1,450Teu than WK44 (before calling USSEA) due to following facts:
Ex USSEA: 850 teu/ Cargo Nos: Additional 200 T/ Agri-products: Additional 400 T

2) AW LANE: L/F: 61%
- AWK lane L/F 54% : AWK lane volume is steadily increasing.
                          Main increased commodity is Agri-product to Taiwan, Indonesia
-  AWS LANE: L/F 70% : After merging with AWY lane, L/F is increasing.

                     Mainly Forest product has been shifted from AWY to AWS lane
3) PN LANE: L/F: 67%
  - Due to small size vessel calling for PNH, the TTL volume has decreased but the L/F shows steady

●  AES :

  - Due to blank sailings of CFN, PSI and ABX, the supply dropped up to 17K, which drove L/F up above 60%.
  - For the next 3~4 weeks, we see very strong booking forecast, which we believe allows BBs to tighten yield management.
  - Taking the 2014 business plan into account, all BBs/BAs are highly requested to focus more on increasing the RPB level
    as high as possible over the course of Q4.
  - The campaign performance of the 1st week is satisfactory to some degree.
    We ask RHQ and BBs once again to pay keen attention to it and attain the targets given at the end.

● IAS :
   - FMX had 2 vssls in the same week.
     Most of cargoes were loaded on the first vssl in WK45 and less cargoes were loaded in WK46.
     Performance decreased temporarily but expect normal vol. from next week again
   - India lane's PFMC in a good tendency, overall L/F of WK46 is 58%.
   - RES PFMC deteriorated for 2 weeks as the side effect of Big Bairam holiday in Arab.
     PFMC will be back to normal level from next week.

● EMS :
   - Bad weather in the sea : LE1 skiped BRITJ, BRSPB. PFMC decreased.
   - No LE3 SVC
   - LW2 PFMC will be normalized from next week. Fishmeal biz in PECLL is now reopened, better PFMC in CLVAP is expected.

[KPI Performance]
[cid:CA92.gif@12345678.87654321]

** For more information, please refer to the attached weekly report

